12	 * {@link AssignCustomerCode} derives the code deterministically from the owner's own fields, so two
13	 * distinct owners can in principle collide. When the assigned code matches an existing owner's
14	 * {@code customerCode}, this step finds the smallest {@code n} of 2 or more that makes it unique and
15	 * applies {@link OwnerCustomerCode#withSuffix} (e.g. {@code NSW-1A2B3C4D} → {@code NSW-1A2B3C4D-2}).
16	 * The suffix spelling lives in {@link OwnerCustomerCode}, which owns the {@code customerCode} format;
17	 * this step contributes only the orchestration — gather existing codes, pick a free {@code n}.
